WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:05.330
Whatever happened to Anna Paquin after escaping
all of the fangbangers, fairies, and werepanthers

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.320
of Bon Temps?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.380
Here's a look at what she's been up to lately.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.940
Small screen complications

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.300
After True Blood, Paquin booked a couple of
TV guest roles, but it still took a few years

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.820
for her to return to the small screen in any
regular capacity.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.880
She took the lead in the 2017 Canadian series
Bellevue, and while the show was well received

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.660
by critics, it was still canceled by CBC after
just one season.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.769
Paquin went on to star in Netflix's adaptation
of Margaret Atwood's novel Alias Grace, but

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:37.260
it didn't receive the same fanfare as The
Handmaid's Tale, another recent Atwood adaptation.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.720
And since Alias Grace was billed as a limited
series, there are few hopes of a second season

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.220
renewal.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.060
In other words, while Paquin has continued
to pursue work on the medium that made her

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.880
a household name, she hasn't yet enjoyed the
type of breakout role she had with True Blood.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.620
No healing power

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.020
Prior to True Blood, Paquin was perhaps best
known for her work as Rogue in the X-Men film

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.520
series.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:03.800
She starred in the original trilogy, and was
among the cast members invited to come back

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.420
to the rebooted franchise for 2014's X-Men:
Days of Future Past.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:12.900
Unfortunately, her scenes were ultimately
edited from the film's theatrical version

00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:17.820
and only made it to screens by way of an expanded
"Rogue Cut" assembled for home video.

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.149
Director Bryan Singer cited the film's length
and crowded plot as his reasons for cutting

00:01:22.149 --> 00:01:22.700
the scenes.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:28.680
Being axed from a successful blockbuster certainly
didn't help to elevate Paquin's profile, even

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.300
if some consider "The Rogue Cut" the best
version of the film.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.900
Pixar's rare miss

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:38.680
One year after Days of Future Past, Paquin
starred as the tough T-rex Ramsey in Pixar's

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.520
The Good Dinosaur.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.000
Despite the studio's long-running track record,
the film was largely ignored by audiences

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.340
and given a comparatively ho-hum reception
by critics as well.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.530
"This is my personal bubble"

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:55.869
Paquin was hardly to blame for The Good Dinosaur's
bad results, as the film's production was

00:01:55.869 --> 00:01:57.540
famously fraught with problems.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:02.960
Even so, suffering through two major letdowns
while working on two large-scale studio films

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.500
had to be a bit demoralizing.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.740
Fighting the mamarazzi machine

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.340
Another reason Paquin may have taken a step
back from the spotlight in recent years is

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:15.140
that she's fiercely protective of her children,
twins Charlie and Poppy.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:20.920
She and her husband, True Blood co-star Stephen
Moyer, welcomed the pair to the world in 2013,

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.780
and she's made a very concerted effort to
guard their privacy.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.640
"I mean they kinda get the concept, cause
they'll see pictures of me or their dad, doing,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.140
'daddy?'"

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.360
Considering Paquin started working at the
age of nine, she's especially familiar with

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.640
how unkind the limelight can be for kids.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.680
She told Today in 2018,

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:42.260
"You won't find any pictures of my children.

00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:43.870
That's a choice we made very specifically.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:46.120
I want the right to say that they're not fair
game."

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.480
Another reason to advocate

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.680
In addition to sticking up for her little
ones, Paquin has also been very vocal on her

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:53.280
own behalf.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.680
In 2010, she publicly revealed that she's
bisexual, appearing in a public service announcement

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.349
for the "Give a Damn" campaign alongside other
celebrities to promote LGBTQ rights and awareness.

00:03:04.349 --> 00:03:09.100
"Because one hate crime is committed approximately
every hour of every day in this country."

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.500
Soon after, she found the subject coming up
repeatedly in interviews, so she felt it was

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.460
important to help spread awareness for bisexuality
on behalf of an oft-misunderstood community.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.470
She's emerged as a major advocate for equal
rights, promoting the NOH8 campaign alongside

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.660
her husband, who has openly supported her.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.440
Reteaming with hubby

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.740
In 2014, Paquin and Moyer joined forces to
start up their own production company, CASM

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:33.260
Films.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:38.540
They landed in familiar territory almost immediately
with a first-look development deal at HBO.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.640
The endeavor might not have resulted in them
reuniting for another romp through the mystical

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.400
wilderness, but the company has allowed them
to explore some other territory.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.680
2018's The Parting Glass was directed by Moyer,
while Paquin, who co-produced, starred in

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:52.320
the picture.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:57.340
It was based on a script from the pair's fellow
True Blood alum, Denis O'Hare, who also appears

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:57.840
in the film.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:02.700
The newest move for Paquin and CASM Films
is a British television series called Flack,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:06.740
which will feature her as an American public
relations executive trying to hack it in London.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.140
Like most of her recent TV work, the series
is expected to be short, with an initial order

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.580
for just six episodes.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.700
Returning to the big time

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:19.100
Although Paquin's been comparatively under
the radar lately, that's likely to change

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.300
in the very near future.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:25.940
She stars alongside Robert De Niro in Martin
Scorsese's upcoming gangster drama The Irishman,

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.980
a project she's described as being directly
in her wheelhouse.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.600
In the film, Paquin portrays Peggy, daughter
of Frank "The Irishman" Sheeran, the mafioso

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.680
who claimed to assassinate Jimmy Hoffa.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.480
The film completed production in March 2018
and is expected to debut on Netflix in 2019.

